1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,437
One More, Please!

3
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:06,510
It's Saturday morning, and the bakery smells amazing.

4
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,906
Warm bread.

5
00:00:07,906 --> 00:00:09,437
Sweet cinnamon.

6
00:00:09,437 --> 00:00:11,114
And something buttery.

7
00:00:11,114 --> 00:00:12,906
Dad smiles at me.

8
00:00:12,906 --> 00:00:15,072
You're ordering today, Lucy.

9
00:00:15,072 --> 00:00:16,187
Me?

10
00:00:16,187 --> 00:00:17,260
Yep.

11
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:18,802
I'll be right here.

12
00:00:18,802 --> 00:00:19,989
Okay.

13
00:00:19,989 --> 00:00:21,520
I can do this.

14
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,749
The woman behind the counter waves.

15
00:00:23,749 --> 00:00:25,010
Hi there!

16
00:00:25,010 --> 00:00:26,562
What can I get for you?

17
00:00:26,562 --> 00:00:29,124
Could I have two cinnamon rolls, please?

18
00:00:29,124 --> 00:00:30,364
Sure!

19
00:00:30,364 --> 00:00:31,937
For here or to go?

20
00:00:31,937 --> 00:00:33,458
I look at Dad.

21
00:00:33,458 --> 00:00:35,770
He points to the little paper bags.

22
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:37,583
To go, please.

23
00:00:37,583 --> 00:00:39,604
The woman reaches for a bag.

24
00:00:39,604 --> 00:00:42,104
Then I remember my little brother, Ben.

25
00:00:42,104 --> 00:00:45,666
He's at home, probably asking Mom when breakfast is coming.

26
00:00:45,666 --> 00:00:47,937
Actually, could we make that three?

27
00:00:47,937 --> 00:00:49,281
Of course.

28
00:00:49,281 --> 00:00:51,166
Three cinnamon rolls.

29
00:00:51,166 --> 00:00:53,093
Dad raises an eyebrow.

30
00:00:53,093 --> 00:00:54,927
Who's the third one for?

31
00:00:54,927 --> 00:00:56,093
Ben!

32
00:00:56,093 --> 00:00:57,385
Good thinking.

33
00:00:57,385 --> 00:01:00,114
He'd notice if we came home smelling like cinnamon.

34
00:01:00,114 --> 00:01:01,489
I laugh.

35
00:01:01,489 --> 00:01:04,739
Then I spot a tray of tiny cookies shaped like cats.

36
00:01:04,739 --> 00:01:06,541
One has a crooked ear.

37
00:01:06,541 --> 00:01:08,989
It looks a little like our cat, Noodle.

38
00:01:08,989 --> 00:01:10,572
Dad, look!

39
00:01:10,572 --> 00:01:12,114
That one's Noodle.

40
00:01:12,114 --> 00:01:13,791
It does look like him.

41
00:01:13,791 --> 00:01:15,708
Can we get a cookie, too?

42
00:01:15,708 --> 00:01:17,489
Dad checks the bag.

43
00:01:17,489 --> 00:01:19,479
Let's stick with the rolls today.

44
00:01:19,479 --> 00:01:20,666
Okay.

45
00:01:20,666 --> 00:01:22,239
Maybe next time.

46
00:01:22,239 --> 00:01:24,395
The woman hands me our breakfast.

47
00:01:24,395 --> 00:01:25,770
How much is it?

48
00:01:25,770 --> 00:01:27,822
Nine dollars, please.

49
00:01:27,822 --> 00:01:30,354
Dad pays, and I take the bag.

50
00:01:30,354 --> 00:01:32,427
It's warm against my fingers.

51
00:01:32,427 --> 00:01:34,812
Could we have a few napkins, please?

52
00:01:34,812 --> 00:01:36,270
Absolutely.

53
00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:37,583
Here you go.

54
00:01:37,583 --> 00:01:38,833
Thank you!

55
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:40,343
Have a nice day!

56
00:01:40,343 --> 00:01:41,854
You, too!

57
00:01:41,854 --> 00:01:44,145
Outside, Dad grins.

58
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:46,083
You handled that really well.

59
00:01:46,083 --> 00:01:47,583
I grin back.

60
00:01:47,583 --> 00:01:50,249
I only forgot Ben for about three seconds.

61
00:01:50,249 --> 00:01:52,760
At home, Ben runs to the door.

62
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,322
Did you get me anything?

63
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:56,020
I hold up the bag.

64
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,729
One cinnamon roll.

65
00:01:57,729 --> 00:01:59,083
Just for you.

66
00:01:59,083 --> 00:02:00,614
You're the best!

67
00:02:00,614 --> 00:02:03,093
Noodle walks over and sniffs the bag.

68
00:02:03,093 --> 00:02:05,374
Sorry, Noodle," I tell him.

69
00:02:05,374 --> 00:02:07,343
Your breakfast is in your bowl.

70
00:02:07,343 --> 00:02:09,718
He flicks his tail and walks away.

71
00:02:09,718 --> 00:02:11,249
Dad laughs.

72
00:02:11,249 --> 00:02:13,512
I think he wants to speak to the manager.
